# CHANGELOG

## 20260816

0.4.1: ~ .gitignore: + current default contents

1. ~ .gitignore: + current default contents


## 20260807

0.4.0: Add a CHANGELOG in the form changelogger writes, and retire the Changes section from the script header.

1. + CHANGELOG. Generated by changelogger from the revisions staged out of the git history, then edited. Tier 1 supplied 0.0.4, 0.2.0, 0.2.2, 0.3.1 and 0.3.2 from their own Changes sections, tier 2 diffed the rest, and tier 3 inventoried 0.0.0.
2. - The Changes section from the script header. The CHANGELOG holds that record now, and keeping both invites them to disagree.
3. Nine summaries are written here, those versions recording none, and are read off the diffs rather than off any prose. Six of the fifteen versions were made on one day.


## 20260807

0.3.2: Make the script executable.

1. ~ bin/skyhooks: mode 100644 --> 100755. A script carrying a shebang and not the bit to go with it cannot be run from a clone at all. Homebrew's bin.install had been setting the bit on the way past, so nothing showed until the formula moved to libexec.install, which keeps whatever mode the repository has.


